---
description: "Verification and honest reporting"
alwaysApply: true
---
**CONFIDENTIALITY:** INTERNAL — verification output must not expose secrets or real sensitive data.

Purpose: Verify behavior with the narrowest meaningful check and report evidence honestly.

Standards:
- Run the narrowest relevant check first, then broaden when useful.
- Report `[run]`, `[not run]`, `[failed]`, and `[unavailable]` checks explicitly.
- Do not claim tests passed unless they ran successfully.
- Add regression tests when practical and record known gaps.

See also: `.cursor/rules/010-agent-execution-contract.mdc`.

Developer usage example: "Run the focused test command, capture PASS/FAIL, and list unavailable integration checks."
